    <h2>Where they go</h2>
    <p class="desc">One dot per county; dot area scales with unit count.
      In the all-types view each county is colored by its dominant type,
      which makes the geography legible at a glance: rural-enhanced yellow
      across the plains and mountain West, neighborhood blue in the
      suburbs, red public-health units in the urban cores. Hover any dot
      for the county's breakdown.</p>
    <span class="mode-toggle" id="units-filter" role="group" aria-label="Unit type filter">
      <button data-type="all" class="active">All types</button>
      <button data-type="a">Type A</button>
