    <div id="units-map" style="margin-top:12px"></div>
    <p class="note" id="units-integrity"></p>
    <details class="tableview"><summary>View allocation by state</summary>
      <div class="tbl-scroll"><table class="data" id="units-state-table"></table></div>
    </details>
    <p class="note">Method limits: this is a capacity plan, not a siting
      study. Within-county placement, drive-time modeling, tribal-land
      coordination, and site-level feasibility all belong to the
      regional planning phase (Phase 4–5). County demand uses
      resident population; commuter and seasonal populations are not
      modeled. The rural floor guarantees a unit even where volume alone
      would not justify one; that is a policy choice about access, priced
      in, not hidden.</p>
